  "answer": "Project Zenith is a high-priority initiative aimed at driving innovation, optimizing cloud storage, and enhancing data analytics and visualization. Key milestones include a kickoff in Q3 2023 (July 15th), a $500,000 budget for Phase One, and a subsequent executive-approved budget of $2M covering R&D and marketing. The project has seen significant progress, including a breakthrough in predictive analytics, successful completion of the testing phase, and updated security protocols. Leadership includes Sarah Tan, Marcus Cole, and Neil. The project is currently seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November, with a detailed report on Phase Two progress to be shared on November 20th. A celebration for the testing milestone occurred on October 10th, and a compliance plan budget of $55,000 has been allocated."
